  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Hands-on Lab",
    "overview": "An approachable science exhibit expressed through ordinary browser controls and inspectable evidence. The approved Squeeze material uses a forest-green working field, a pale encounter stage, peach actions, and rounded heavy headings. Playfulness comes from the type and explicit action marks; explanations remain direct and conditional.\n\nThis is a scan of the implemented source, not a new direction. `PRODUCT.md` owns product truth; the Hands-on Lab surface contract owns its reading order. “Game Theory” remains a working label. Historical static alternatives do not define this system.\n\nUsability revision: one question and run action precede a plain-language cooperation finding. Optional settings, strategy scores, variation, and encounter replay are separately expandable. The playable introduction and simulation rules remain unchanged.\n\nThe latest user-confirmed result hierarchy leads with six persistent strategy avatars and raw cumulative points after N rounds across all tournament games. Five rounded nice identities contrast with angular Always Defect. Nice means never defects first in error-free play. Cooperation and weighted averages remain expandable; scores show playing time and fixed-schedule limitations. Source art, exact prompts and current screenshots are tracked in the repository.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Chromatic working field and a pale, legible encounter stage.",
      "Heavy rounded headings paired with compact, readable explanations.",
      "Familiar controls and explicit, colour-independent C/D action marks.",
      "Measured results, their conditions, and their limitations remain inspectable."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Grounds Rule",
        "body": "Use the ink pair belonging to the current ground; pale stages must not inherit the page's pale text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Explicit Action Rule",
        "body": "Pair C/D symbols with their written meanings and earned points; colour is not the sole carrier of the distinction.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Evidence Rule",
        "body": "Use ground changes and rules to separate evidence; do not introduce raised-card stacks into this incumbent surface.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the matching forest or pale-surface ink pair and visible keyboard focus.",
      "**Do** preserve explicit action meanings, labelled conditions, table captions, and local scroll affordances.",
      "**Do** keep findings qualified and distinguish the opening illustration from completed tournament evidence.",
      "**Do** reuse the self-hosted heading/body pairing and compact spacing rhythm."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** encode cooperate/defect or runtime status through colour alone.",
      "**Don't** turn historical static alternatives or unused source tokens into new visual authority.",
      "**Don't** present the design scan as deployment, formal accessibility approval, physical-device validation, or beginner-comprehension evidence."
    ]
  }
}
